ook"}, "contributor": "encyclopedia:cia-world-factbook", "license": "public-domain", "license_url": "https://www.cia.gov/the-world-factbook/about/copyright-and-contributors/", "source_url": "https://www.cia.gov/the-world-factbook/countries/ml/", "revision": "factbook.json", "historical": false}, {"id": "enc-cia-ml-25", "text": "The junta then established a transition government and appointed Bah N’DAW, a retired army officer and former defense minister, as interim president and Colonel Assimi GOITA, the coup leader and chairman of the CNSP, as interim vice president.", "tier": "anchor", "state": "anchor", "trust": "trusted", "sfe": {"Phi": 1, "eps": 0.0, "mu": 1.0}, "packet": {"schema": "FORGE-RESONANCE-PACKET/v1", "Phi": 1, "eps": 0.0, "mu": 1.0, "sfe": {"Phi": 1, "eps": 0.0, "mu": 1.0}, "placed_by": "athena", "standing": "anchor", "phi_basis": "ingestion placement; factual anchor, phase Φ1"}, "concepts": ["A.MALI"], "concept": "A.MALI", "provenance": {"source": "cia-world-factbook", "source_url": "https://www.cia.gov/the-world-factbook/countries/ml/", "revision": "factbook.json", "license": "public-domain", "license_url": "https://www.cia.gov/the-world-factbook/about/copyright-and-contributors/", "terms": "https://www.usa.gov/government-works", "historical": false, "ingestion_note": "Sentence cut at ingestion from the CIA World Factbook. The factbook.json mirror is CC0. Recall does not segment text.", "contributor": "encyclopedia:cia-world-factbook"}, "contributor": "encyclopedia:cia-world-factbook", "license": "public-domain", "license_url": "https://www.cia.gov/the-world-factbook/about/copyright-and-contributors/", "source_url": "https://www.cia.gov/the-world-factbook/countries/ml/", "revision": "factbook.json", "historical": false}, {"id": "enc-cia-ml-26", "text": "The transition government’s charter allowed it to rule for up to 18 months before calling a general election.", "tier": "anchor", "state": "anchor", "trust": "trusted", "sfe": {"Phi": 1, "eps": 0.0, "mu": 1.0}, "packet": {"schema": "FORGE-RESONANCE-PACKET/v1", "Phi": 1, "eps": 0.0, "mu": 1.0, "sfe": {"Phi": 1, "eps": 0.0, "mu": 1.0}, "placed_by": "athena", "standing": "anchor", "phi_basis": "ingestion placement; factual anchor, phase Φ1"}, "concepts": ["A.MALI"], "concept": "A.MALI", "provenance": {"source": "cia-world-factbook", "source_url": "https://www.cia.gov/the-world-factbook/countries/ml/", "revision": "factbook.json", "license": "public-domain", "license_url": "https://www.cia.gov/the-world-factbook/about/copyright-and-contributors/", "terms": "https://www.usa.gov/government-works", "historical": false, "ingestion_note": "Sentence cut at ingestion from the CIA World Factbook. The factbook.json mirror is CC0. Recall does not segment text.", "contributor": "encyclopedia:cia-world-factbook"}, "contributor": "encyclopedia:cia-world-factbook", "license": "public-domain", "license_url": "https://www.cia.gov/the-world-factbook/about/copyright-and-contributors/", "source_url": "https://www.cia.gov/the-world-factbook/countries/ml/", "revision": "factbook.json", "historical": false}, {"id": "enc-cia-ml-27", "text": "In 2021, GOITA led a military takeover, arresting the interim president after a Cabinet shake-up removed GOITA’s key allies.", "tier": "anchor", "state": "anchor", "trust": "trusted", "sfe": {"Phi": 1, "eps": 0.0, "mu": 1.0}, "packet": {"schema": "FORGE-RESONANCE-PACKET/v1", "Phi": 1, "eps": 0.0, "mu": 1.0, "sfe": {"Phi": 1, "eps": 0.0, "mu": 1.0}, "placed_by": "athena", "standing": "anchor", "phi_basis": "ingestion placement; factual anchor, phase Φ1"}, "concepts": ["A.MALI"], "concept": "A.MALI", "provenance": {"source": "cia-world-factbook", "source_url": "https://www.cia.gov/the-world-factbook/countries/ml/", "revision": "factbook.json", "license": "public-domain", "license_url": "https://www.cia.gov/the-world-factbook/about/copyright-and-contributors/", "terms": "https://www.usa.gov/government-works", "historical": false, "ingestion_note": "Sentence cut at ingestion from the CIA World Factbook. The factbook.json mirror is CC0. Recall does not segment text.", "contributor": "encyclopedia:cia-world-factbook"}, "contributor": "encyclopedia:cia-world-factbook", "license": "public-domain", "license_url": "https://www.cia.gov/the-world-factbook/about/copyright-and-contributors/", "source_url": "https://www.cia.gov/the-world-factbook/countries/ml/", "revision": "factbook.json", "historical": false}, {"id": "enc-cia-ml-28", "text": "GOITA was sworn in as transition president, and Choguel Kokalla MAIGA was sworn in as prime minister.", "tier": "anchor", "state": "anchor", "trust": "trusted", "sfe": {"Phi": 1, "eps": 0.0, "mu": 1.0}, "packet": {"schema": "FORGE-RESONANCE-PACKET/v1", "Phi": 1, "eps": 0.0, "mu": 1.0, "sfe": {"Phi": 1, "eps": 0.0, "mu": 1.0}, "placed_by": "athena", "standing": "anchor", "phi_basis": "ingestion placement; factual anchor, phase Φ1"}, "concepts": ["A.MALI"], "concept": "A.MALI", "provenance": {"source": "cia-world-factbook", "source_url": "https://www.cia.gov/the-world-factbook/countries/ml/", "revision": "factbook.json", "license": "public-domain", "license_url": "https://www.cia.gov/the-world-factbook/about/copyright-and-contributors/", "terms": "https://www.usa.gov/government-works", "historical": false, "ingestion_note": "Sentence cut at ingestion from the CIA World Factbook. The factbook.json mirror is CC0. Recall does not segment text.", "contributor": "encyclopedia:cia-world-factbook"}, "contributor": "encyclopedia:cia-world-factbook", "license": "public-domain", "license_url": "https://www.cia.gov/the-world-factbook/about/copyright-and-contributors/", "source_url": "https://www.cia.gov/the-world-factbook/countries/ml/", "revision": "factbook.json", "historical": false}, {"id": "enc-cia-ml-29", "text": "In 2022, the Economic Community of West African States (ECOWAS) imposed sanctions on the transition government, and member states closed their borders with Mali after the transition government presented a five-year extension to the electoral calendar.", "tier": "anchor", "state": "anchor", "trust": "trusted", "sfe": {"Phi": 1, "eps": 0.0, "mu": 1.0}, "packet": {"schema": "FORGE-RESONANCE-PACKET/v1", "Phi": 1, "eps": 0.0, "mu": 1.0, "sfe": {"Phi": 1, "eps": 0.0, "mu": 1.0}, "placed_by": "athena", "standing": "anchor", "phi_basis": "ingestion placement; factual anchor, phase Φ1"}, "concepts": ["A.MALI"], "concept": "A.MALI", "provenance": {"source": "cia-world-factbook", "source_url": "https://www.cia.gov/the-world-factbook/countries/ml/", "revision": "factbook.json", "license": "public-domain", "license_url": "https://www.cia.gov/the-world-factbook/about/copyright-and-contributors/", "terms": "https://www.usa.gov/government-works", "historical": false, "ingestion_note": "Sentence cut at ingestion from the CIA World Factbook. The factbook.json mirror is CC0. Recall does not segment text.", "contributor": "encyclopedia:cia-world-factbook"}, "contributor": "encyclopedia:cia-world-factbook", "license": "public-domain", "license_url": "https://www.cia.gov/the-world-factbook/about/copyright-and-contributors/", "source_url": "https://www.cia.gov/the-world-factbook/countries/ml/", "revision": "factbook.json", "historical": false}, {"id": "enc-cia-ml-3", "text": "Primarily a trading empire, Mali derived its wealth from gold and maintained several goldfields and trade routes in the Sahel.", "tier": "anchor", "state": "anchor", "trust": "trusted", "sfe": {"Phi": 1, "eps": 0.0, "mu": 1.0}, "packet": {"schema": "FORGE-RESONANCE-PACKET/v1", "Phi": 1, "eps": 0.0, "mu": 1.0, "sfe": {"Phi": 1, "eps": 0.0, "mu": 1.0}, "placed_by": "athena", "standing": "anchor", "phi_basis": "ingestion placement; factual anchor, phase Φ1"}, "concepts": ["A.MALI"], "concept": "A.MALI", "provenance": {"source": "cia-world-factbook", "source_url": "https://www.cia.gov/the-world-factbook/countries/ml/", "revision": "factbook.json", "license": "public-domain", "license_url": "https:/